  "description": "Twelve 3 mm wide satin rectangles with lengths 0.5, 0.8, 1.0, 1.2, 1.5, 2, 3, 5, 8, 10, 12, 15 mm, 7 mm apart, direction 0 (rows along x, so the crossings run across the 3 mm width and the length is the swept parameter), density 4.5, under sewing off. Issue #122: whether the extra end crossing threshold is 1 mm or 10 mm. PE-DESIGN's needle points per column (tie-in and lock included): 0.5 mm -> 15, 0.8 mm -> 12, 1.0 mm -> 17, 1.2 mm -> 17, 1.5 mm -> 16, 2 mm -> 23, 3 mm -> 28, 5 mm -> 36, 8 mm -> 44, 10 mm -> 63, 12 mm -> 66, 15 mm -> 87; 424 in all. The total count and bounds are compared; the per-column counts are in the manifest for the satin track.",
